<Docs title="Brand" group="Foundations" lead="dawn & dusk is cxkw.dev’s system: warm interior neutrals, a golden-hour accent, and a heavy lowercase voice.">
  <h2 id="idea">The idea</h2>
  <p>Two moods of the same place. <b>Dawn</b> is cream paper, greige walls and ink; <b>dusk</b> is the same room after sunset — warm near-black, cream type, and the last apricot light. Every component is designed for both from the start.</p>
  <h2 id="principles">Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Quiet by default.</b> Tone instead of borders, one accent at a time, generous space.</li>
    <li><b>Warm, not beige.</b> Greige neutrals with golden-hour colour for what matters.</li>
    <li><b>Loud headlines, calm everything else.</b> The lockup is the voice; Figtree does the work.</li>
    <li><b>Data is a first-class citizen.</b> Dense tables, mono figures and clear status are part of the system, not an afterthought.</li>
    <li><b>Built for agents too.</b> Plain HTML classes and tokens an assistant can apply correctly — see the <a href="../skill">agent skill</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2 id="logo">Logo</h2>
  <p>The wordmark is the two-line <b>dawn &amp; dusk</b> lockup set in Outfit 800 with the second line cut out of the first. Use the one-line version in tight horizontal spaces. Clear space, sizes and colour use are on the <a href="../components/logo">Logo</a> page.</p>
  <h2 id="voice">Voice</h2>
  <Guides do={['Short, lowercase headlines: “ship at dusk”, “the lab”.', 'Plain verbs on buttons.', 'Numbers and IDs in mono.']} dont={['Don’t use exclamation marks in UI.', 'Don’t title-case everything.']} />
</Docs>
